title: Congressional Leadership Elections
subtitle: Can the Establishment be challenged?
view-if: year = 2018 and election_already_held = 1
max-visits: 1
tags: event

= Congressional Leadership Elections

Now that the general election is decided, it's time to decide the new direction of the Party in National Politics.

There are 2 major leadership elections. We'll begin with the Senate.

- @senate: The Senate Minority Leader

@senate

Chuck Schumer stands as a juggernaut in the Senate. A Senator willing to challenge him is hard to come by.

- @schumer
- @no_schumer

@schumer
title: Chuck Schumer for Minority Leader
subtitle: The presumptive nominee

Chuck Schumer is given two more years as Senate Minority Leader. What's going on in the House?

- @house: The Speaker of the House Elections

@no_schumer
title: We can't give Schumer two more years.
choose-if: populism > 80
subtitle: He is the reason we lost, after all.
unavailable-subtitle: The Establishment's influence is too great

WIP

- @house: The Speaker of the House Elections

@house

With our newfound House Majority, it's up to us to determine the Speaker of the House of Representatives. Nancy Pelosi is powerful, but could she be usurped?

- @pelosi
- @ryan

@pelosi
title: Nancy Pelosi for Speaker
subtitle: The Establishment's pick

Unsurprisingly, Nancy Pelosi has returned to the Speakership after more than a decade. 

@ryan
title: Could Tim Ryan be persuaded to challenge Pelosi once more?
choose-if: populism >= 60
unavailable-subtitle: There just isn't enough opposiition to Pelosi to justify a challenge.

Tim Ryan has been persuaded to make a formal bid for Speaker of the House! The question remains, however: does he have the support of the House Democratic Conference?

- @yes: He does!
- @no: He does not!

@yes
view-if: populism > 70

Amazingly, Tim Ryan has won the Speakership election! The defeat of Pelosi marks a major shift in the attitude of the national Democratic Party.

@no
view-if: populism < 70

Unfortunately, but perhaps unsurprisingly, Ryan was unable to usurp Pelosi despite a fierce leadership struggle.
